A||||10||frontal lobe||Fiero stars in the evening news!||||1||
Z||000000||frontal lobe||03-01-2001||11:10 AM||||Local tv newscast in Milwaukee this week had a story about a state law where you can recover damages if you are a victim of vandalism, obviously if they catch the person.  So this lady is driving along minding her own business one night and some kids drive up next to her and egg her car.  She is obviously scared and upset but still has the presence of mind to get the license plate.  She calls the police on her cell phone and the police look around and catch the guys.  A search of their car reveals a receipt from a grocery store for the purchase of 3 dozen eggs that very night!  The search also reveals a video camera!  Police view the videotape and THE GUYS HAD RECORDED THEMSELVES EGGING HER CAR!  Duhhh!  Busted.  They then went on to show how her paint had peeled off her car all over the place where the eggs had hit, and she needed almost 3,000 in paint work, etc.  They went on to show the struggle they had to get the money, but finally got it after 10 months of going to court, etc.<P>Anyway, part of the story was that they were working so hard to get the money because the car was their beloved 1988 FIERO!  They actually showed the videotape of poor Fiero being egged, and then after pictures of the paint peeled off.  Pretty awesome story.||||reg||1
Z||000001||bHooper||03-01-2001||02:34 PM||||poor lady!<P>but nice for the fiero to get some tv coverage!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||03-01-2001||02:48 PM||||Well, I'm glad she finally got some satisfaction.  Crazy guys should have known you can't cook eggs very well on the 1988 models.  The 1984 models at least have the nice "grille" hood for BBQing steaks, but eggs? C'mon...<P>Receipts and videotape footage?!  Maybe I'm sick or something, but I really enjoy the "stupid criminal" stories  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   ||||reg||6
