Z||000007||Huck||03-01-2001||06:57 PM||||heh... I know what you mean.  Dont mess with Fiero Folk!  An EX-friend backed into my 87GT in september...  He told me he would pay for it.. my first quote was to just have the front end repaired (there was a hole in it from the trailer hitch of his truck).  He tried to screw me by only offering me half, so I went and got another quote to geta brand new front end.  It all dragged on for awhile,  but I finally ended up getting $1050 out of him insted of $450 which is where we started at... and Im getting my car fixed right.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Next time he'll know better than to run over a fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Huck||||reg||1
Z||000008||frontal lobe||03-01-2001||07:06 PM||||ChadMan, have to settle for the Vise-Grips clamping on to the wallet.  Pretty expensive eggs:  89cents per dozen x 3 dozen, PLUS the $2,850 payment comes to $950.89 per dozen.<P>Wish you could see the video.  They are driving along beside the Fiero--them in the left lane, Fiero in the right.  You can clearly see she is driving a silver Fiero notchback.  Then you see an egg flying through the air hitting the Fiero just in front of the driver's mirror.  Lots of whooping going on in the car.  It was a heinous act of cowardice and painful to watch, but it was like in those Fox network "amazing video" shows:  "Watch again!"<P>You are right.  For a lesser car, after that much court time, a person may have caved in and said, oh just forget it.  But NOT a Fiero owner!||||reg||1
